pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowHierarchyOfNeedsSeries a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Maslow's hierarchy of human needs"@en, "Maslows Hierarchie der menschlichen Bedürfnisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "The seven levels of need that Hine, in the Commentary to Howling, takes from the psychologist Abraham Maslow as the frame of the demon hierarchy of his retirement: biological, safety, affiliative, esteem, cognitive, aesthetic and self-actualization, a pyramid running from bodily survival to more complex needs."@en ;
    skos:note "The order is Maslow's, ascribed to him by Hine, and imported into the practice of the Babblogue as its frame; it is not an order Hine devised. Hine's own three-level demon hierarchy built on it stands in Oven-Ready Chaos."@en, "Hine reports this from Abraham Maslow; the node holds his report, and the named work, reachable in its own right, is not read through him."@en, "Differs from pmc:ChaosMagicOrcMaslowDemonHierarchy (Oven-Ready Chaos, text of 1992): the Oven-Ready series is Hine's own three-level demon hierarchy (survival, ego, abstract); here, in the Commentary of this version, the seven levels of Maslow's hierarchy of needs as Hine prints them, the order ascribed to Maslow."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowBiologicalNeeds ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowSafetyNeeds ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowAffiliativeNeeds ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowEsteemNeeds ;
    rdf:_5 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowCognitiveNeeds ;
    rdf:_6 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowAestheticNeeds ;
    rdf:_7 pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowSelfActualization ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Maslow's hierarchy as Hine reports it orders needs from bodily survival up to self-knowledge, and each level has its sense from its place: those of one level have to be met at least in part before the next level comes to matter, so that a starving person gives little weight to aesthetic needs." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AspectsOfEvocation ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Aspects of Evocation: Collected Essays (version 1.1, dated March 1988 in the text, introduction signed March 1998), Howling, Commentary, The Hierarchy of Human Needs, page unmarked in text layer; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item phil-hine-aspects-of-evocation" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowBiologicalNeeds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Biological needs (Maslow level 1)"@en, "Biologische Bedürfnisse (Maslow, Stufe 1)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first and most basic level as Hine prints the hierarchy: bodily needs such as food and drink and being warm."@en ;
    skos:note "Member 1 of pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowHierarchyOfNeedsSeries. The text layer prints the level names in one column and their glosses in another; the pairing follows the line order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AspectsOfEvocation ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Aspects of Evocation: Collected Essays (version 1.1, dated March 1988 in the text, introduction signed March 1998), Howling, Commentary, The Hierarchy of Human Needs, page unmarked in text layer; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item phil-hine-aspects-of-evocation" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowSafetyNeeds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Safety needs (Maslow level 2)"@en, "Sicherheitsbedürfnisse (Maslow, Stufe 2)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second level as Hine prints the hierarchy: safety, glossed as being free of fear."@en ;
    skos:note "Member 2 of pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowHierarchyOfNeedsSeries."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AspectsOfEvocation ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Aspects of Evocation: Collected Essays (version 1.1, dated March 1988 in the text, introduction signed March 1998), Howling, Commentary, The Hierarchy of Human Needs, page unmarked in text layer; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item phil-hine-aspects-of-evocation" .

pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowAffiliativeNeeds a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Affiliative needs (Maslow level 3)"@en, "Zugehörigkeitsbedürfnisse (Maslow, Stufe 3)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third level as Hine prints the hierarchy: the need to be treated with consideration by others."@en ;
    skos:note "Member 3 of pmc:ChaosMagicAoeMaslowHierarchyOfNeedsSeries."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:ChaosMagic ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AspectsOfEvocation ;
    dcterms:source "Hine, Aspects of Evocation: Collected Essays (version 1.1, dated March 1988 in the text, introduction signed March 1998), Howling, Commentary, The Hierarchy of Human Needs, page unmarked in text layer; read in the full-text layer of the archive.org item phil-hine-aspects-of-evocation" .

